{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02322",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.59,
      "end_seconds": 5.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Morning, um, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.06,
      "end_seconds": 12.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.29,
      "end_seconds": 16.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Well, I've been having yellow eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.07,
      "end_seconds": 23.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.13,
      "end_seconds": 37.86,
      "duration_seconds": 13.73,
      "text": "Honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, I really can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.09,
      "end_seconds": 41.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "I follow. Alright, is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.26,
      "end_seconds": 45.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "It usually comes with dark urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.0,
      "end_seconds": 48.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Has there been pale stools too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.38,
      "end_seconds": 52.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Yeah. One week, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.67,
      "end_seconds": 58.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Have you had yellow eyes before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.51,
      "end_seconds": 67.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "A bit, a couple of years ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.96,
      "end_seconds": 85.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.81,
      "end_seconds": 90.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.01,
      "end_seconds": 94.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.11,
      "end_seconds": 101.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.81,
      "text": "Actually, I've had gout, yes. Yes, heart failure. I've had heart disease, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.09,
      "end_seconds": 110.3,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "Yes. Right, so gout is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.44,
      "end_seconds": 123.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.23,
      "end_seconds": 131.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.1,
      "end_seconds": 137.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.1,
      "end_seconds": 149.42,
      "duration_seconds": 11.32,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.73,
      "end_seconds": 153.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.97,
      "end_seconds": 162.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.99,
      "text": "Febuxostat. I take it 80 milligrams, once a day for the gout. Spironolactone, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.97,
      "end_seconds": 166.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.02,
      "end_seconds": 173.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "25 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.58,
      "end_seconds": 177.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.61,
      "end_seconds": 187.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "About about three months. Aspirin. I take it 75 milligrams, once a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.11,
      "end_seconds": 190.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Okay, any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.42,
      "end_seconds": 200.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "I had a triple bypass eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.88,
      "end_seconds": 217.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Okay, a few quick ones: itching, confusion, high fever or vomiting blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.51,
      "end_seconds": 220.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.65,
      "end_seconds": 223.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.76,
      "end_seconds": 228.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.48,
      "end_seconds": 233.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.03,
      "end_seconds": 249.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.83,
      "end_seconds": 273.38,
      "duration_seconds": 9.55,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 74, temperature 36.7. And blood pressure 126 over 71, weight 80 kilos, height 158 centimetres, oxygen saturation is 99 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.61,
      "end_seconds": 279.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.01,
      "end_seconds": 285.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.51,
      "end_seconds": 288.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.26,
      "end_seconds": 311.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "The whites of the eyes are yellow and the liver edge is tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.45,
      "end_seconds": 333.49,
      "duration_seconds": 20.04,
      "text": "Please sit back down. So, based on the history and the examination, I'm honestly not certain yet. It could be acute hepatitis, possibly hepatitis A after travel, or it might be a gallstone blockage. Just to be sure I understood. You've had yellow eyes, and no confusion or high fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.56,
      "end_seconds": 336.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.83,
      "end_seconds": 371.95,
      "duration_seconds": 35.12,
      "text": "Let's book a hepatitis screen to look into jaundice. We should do liver blood tests for jaundice. Rest, avoid alcohol and wash your hands carefully, as it can spread. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. Do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse. Book a review in one week. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.63,
      "end_seconds": 376.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}